window.MSB=window.MSB||{};MSB["lider-en"]=[["Leadership is the ability to find the strength within yourself to influence others, whether you were born a leader or became one along the way. We usually picture true leaders as people gifted with charisma, self-confidence and the ability to make important decisions with ease. Yet we often forget that leadership is not so much a calling as a set of qualities and skills acquired over the course of a life.","In this book, «A Leader Not by Calling», we will look at the other side of the coin — the side that says leadership can be the fruit of self-improvement, growth and the ability to see potential in yourself. We will dive into the stories of different people who faced challenges and crises, yet answered them not with fear but with faith in their own abilities.","This book will be your guide into the world of leadership, where we will show that every person can be a leader if only they can overcome their inner obstacles and learn to move forward with confidence. We will uncover the secrets of successful leaders that will help you find in yourself the strength and motivation to reach great goals.","So if you want to learn how to turn your challenges into opportunities, how to find your own leadership potential and how to influence others by bringing positive change, we invite you on an exciting journey into the world of leadership. «A Leader Not by Calling» is your step towards a successful future, where crises turn into great victories and you become a true leader of your own life."],["We often picture true leaders as people born with extraordinary abilities — focused, brave and decisive. In our imagination, such people are gifted with a special calling for life. We cannot even guess what amazing adventures might become their destiny. We recall the stories of great leaders who changed the course of history, like Moses, Isaiah, Gideon and many others, and it seems they were gifted with a calling from birth. It seems that every true leader met angels, saw supernatural signs or heard the voice of God. That is exactly how we tend to see the great leaders of the Bible. Yet among them are many who had no experience of a supernatural calling; on the contrary, they doubted their own abilities, and still they became great leaders who changed the world. To see leadership only as something given at birth or through dramatic events is a mistake. Such a view of leadership can affect our self-esteem and our belief that we are able to lead. We may feel that no such special mission or calling was given to us. But is it possible to become a leader through life, growth and development, without dramatic revelations or a call from heaven? Can we, ordinary people, become outstanding leaders without seeing angels or supernatural signs?","The Bible contains examples of people who had no remarkable revelations, visions or angels, yet became outstanding leaders. One of them is Nehemiah. He was an ordinary man serving in the palace of the Persian king Artaxerxes. But when Nehemiah heard about the walls of Jerusalem lying in ruins, his heart was filled with grief. That situation became a challenge for him, and Nehemiah saw his calling in it. He left his comfortable place at the royal court, returned to Jerusalem and took on the rebuilding of the walls. Through his drive as a leader, his energy and determination, Nehemiah was able to unite the people and accomplish a great feat — the restoration of Jerusalem's walls.","So leadership is not only about recognising a calling from birth; it is also the possibility of growing as a leader throughout your life. Each of us carries the potential to become a leader by answering these questions: what matters to us, what makes our heart beat faster, and what could change the world around us. May the story of Nehemiah inspire us to trust our inner convictions and to strive for achievement, regardless of circumstances or remarkable revelations. Each of us can become a leader, raise our banner high and influence the world around us.","«The words of Nehemiah the son of Hachaliah. And it came to pass in the month Chisleu, in the twentieth year, as I was in Shushan the palace, that Hanani, one of my brethren, came, he and certain men of Judah; and I asked them concerning the Jews that had escaped, which were left of the captivity, and concerning Jerusalem. And they said unto me, The remnant that are left of the captivity there in the province are in great affliction and reproach: the wall of Jerusalem also is broken down, and the gates thereof are burned with fire.","And it came to pass, when I heard these words, that I sat down and wept, and mourned certain days, and fasted, and prayed before the God of heaven.» Nehemiah 1:1–4.","My own story may serve as an example for many who have ever felt inclined to avoid leadership roles and public attention. I never thought I would be able to inspire and lift people up from the pulpit, or become a leader for pastors and other leaders. But looking at the fruit of my life and ministry, I realise that I have become a leader for many people.","This path became a real discovery for me, and it changed my life. I had to discover a new, unfamiliar side of myself and go through a rebuilding: from a man who always avoided publicity, leadership and responsibility, to a man who saw his calling from God. I was able to discover gifts and talents in myself that had been hidden from me until then.","My story shows that leadership can open up along the way, at an unexpected moment in our lives, if we respond to the needs of the time. What matters is to move forward with confidence and faith, to believe in yourself as you find your inner challenge and calling. Each of us can be a leader if only we find the strength and the will to open ourselves to new opportunities and walk our unique path with confidence. Leadership is about confidence in your path, devotion to your goals and, above all, faith in God, who always supports us in our efforts.","I understand that my confession may come as a surprise to many, but the truth is that I have always been someone who avoided other people's attention. My inner world always interested me more than socialising with others. I never saw myself as a leader or as someone who could take an active public role. But God has His own sense of humour, and He decided that I should come to enjoy diving into a life of active influence among people. The hardest part for me was the transformation from a person who had guarded his personal space all his life into a leader who has to be open to others. It was a difficult and long process. For a long time I was tempted to trade my calling to lead for a return to my comfortable inner world, far from people's eyes. The full stop in this struggle was put by the words of the Lord:","«Except a corn of wheat fall into the ground and die, it abideth alone: but if it die, it bringeth forth much fruit.","He that loveth his life shall lose it.» John 12:24–25.","For me this became a light in the maze of my endless thoughts and hesitations: could I be a leader if by nature I felt like a different person, one who longed far more for a life that belonged entirely to me? Did I want this; could I become a different person, one able to give his life to God?","«He that loveth his life» was a challenge for me, but a challenge that holds endless good, because it comes from a love for life and a love for me. To keep my life to myself meant to keep everything that was valuable only to me, that gave comfort only to me, that put only my needs at the centre. The truth is that in that case a person eventually loses everything: their calling, their comfortable life and, most importantly, the meaning of their life. We do not always realise that happiness lies not only in comfort and material things but in our life gaining meaning and creative fulfilment. «It bringeth forth much fruit»: we receive a completely different kind of happiness and peace, one that comes when we see the fruit of our work, the fulfilment of what is worth living for. It is a completely different taste of happiness and peace. It does not depend on circumstances or on the presence of challenges; it lives inside you, and once you have tasted it, you will not want to give it up. The true meaning of life is not in hiding from it but in living a real life to the full.","The nature of leadership is always a subject of debate: does it begin at birth, or is it gained through acquired skills and decisions? Our idea of leaders is often tied to innate abilities, charisma and calling. But is that really so? Are leaders born or made?","Some people seem to be born with an undeniable calling to lead. They naturally draw people to themselves, they can influence others' decisions and move them to action. Such personalities are endowed with natural charisma, which attracts with a captivating force. Yet leadership is not only a calling; it is also the gaining of skills and constant growth. Many great leaders of their time travelled the road from insecurity to positions of influence. Their stories can inspire us to see leadership potential in ourselves. One such example is Nehemiah's path as a leader. Although he was not born with unmatched charisma, he recognised his responsibility and was open to growing as a leader. When the news about the state of Jerusalem reached him, Nehemiah felt an inner call to step in and help. He gathered his courage and took responsibility for rebuilding the city, talking with the people and with wise advisers in order to take the necessary steps.","It is important to understand that leadership can be both innate and developed. Every person has their own path in developing leadership qualities, and it can combine an inborn calling with a desire to achieve more.","So whether we are born leaders or become leaders is not the deciding factor. What matters is understanding that every person can grow as a leader if they deeply understand their values and calling, learn responsibility, accept challenges and learn from their mistakes.","Leadership is constant growth, movement and opportunity for each of us. Everyone has their own path to becoming a leader — charismatic, inspired and influential."],["A leader is someone who influences others and is able to inspire, motivate and lead a group of people towards a shared goal. A leader has the abilities and charisma needed to lead others, build effective teams and achieve results. But do you need special character traits to become a true leader? We usually picture someone who was born with the full set of leadership qualities: standing out from others, always at the centre of attention, with a sense of being exceptional and full of self-confidence. Most people cannot boast such gifts, so they tend to think of themselves as unfit to lead. And what about leaders who seemed quiet and, at first glance, had no special charisma that draws attention from the very first second? History knows many examples of people who at first did not stand out at all, yet changed people's lives through their actions and influence.","Mother Teresa became an example of leadership born not of charisma or natural qualities but grown out of faith, devotion and a deep desire to help others. She taught us that true leadership is the readiness to serve, to sacrifice and to show mercy to all people, regardless of their status or social position. Her legacy remains forever remembered as a symbol of hope and love for all humanity.","One example of leadership in business that is striking in its modesty and devotion to service is Warren Buffett, the well-known American investor and entrepreneur. He is one of the richest people in the world, yet in his style of management and his approach to business he has always remained modest and simple.","Buffett remains a humble, simple man who does not loudly celebrate his achievements. He does not make himself into a star or an ideal.","As we can see, a true leader does not always look like a star or someone who stands out from others by external advantages.","Leadership is not limited to positions or titles. Many people can be leaders in their actions, influence those around them and be an example for others, even without a formal leadership position.","The main trait of a true leader is faith in people's potential and the ability to support others and help them grow and succeed. A leader is not simply the one who directs but the one who inspires and helps each member of the team discover their best qualities and abilities.","Leadership is not the gifts a person is born with but the fruit their life bears. It does not matter how well such a person can impress others with their exceptional qualities and their ability to stand out. Many leaders may go unnoticed at first glance, yet they remain influential. Leadership is first of all about inner qualities, not outward ones.","The apostle Paul, so well known to us, is one of the most outstanding and influential figures of Christianity. His story is an amazing example of how an ordinary person can become a leader through faith, conviction and devotion.","At first Paul was known as Saul. He was a Pharisee who opposed Christianity and persecuted Christians. But everything changed when Saul encountered Jesus Christ. On the road to Damascus a bright light from heaven shone around him, and he heard a voice speaking to him. In that encounter he became a Christian and a convinced follower of Christ.","After this transformation Paul became not only a leader in the early church but also one of the most active messengers of Christianity. He made three great missionary journeys through the cities of that time, visiting many regions and peoples. Paul preached the Word of God, founding Christian communities and teaching people about love, mercy and salvation through Jesus Christ.","Paul was an intellectual. He had a deep knowledge of the sacred texts of his time and the ability to reason for his teaching. He wrote many letters to church communities, which became part of the New Testament and remain a valuable source of faith and teaching for Christians to this day.","The apostle Paul became an example of devotion, sacrifice and courage. He faced many hardships, including persecution, prison and danger to his life, but he never betrayed his convictions and preached the Word of God even in the hardest times.","The story of the apostle Paul is a great inspiration for those who doubt their own ability to lead. It shows that even an ordinary person can become a great leader if they have faith, devotion and a readiness to serve others.","Paul wrote about himself:","«For his letters, say they, are weighty and powerful; but his bodily presence is weak, and his speech contemptible.» 2 Corinthians 10:10.","In person Paul did not look the way those who knew him from his letters expected. In a culture that had its own models of orators, thinkers and leaders, the appearance of a Jewish preacher who did not impress by his looks was a stumbling block for some. But Paul insists that he has the power and grace to be an apostle despite the expectations of those for whom the measure of leadership is outward appearance. Paul goes on to say that he does not compare himself with others; the only measure of his leadership is the work he does and the fruit his preaching of the Gospel bears. He considered himself the least of the apostles:","«For I am the least of the apostles, that am not meet to be called an apostle…","But by the grace of God I am what I am: and his grace which was bestowed upon me was not in vain; but I laboured more abundantly than they all: yet not I, but the grace of God which was with me.» 1 Corinthians 15:9–10.","This view of leadership may differ from the common belief that a true leader is a «superhero», a model of perfection and flawlessness, someone who never knows doubt or inner hesitation.","This should inspire us to move towards leadership in our own lives. Do not consider yourself unable to lead just because you feel unsure of yourself or lack experience, competence or other qualities. All of these can be gained through learning and through experience. Naturally quiet or modest people can remember the examples in this chapter. Your weaknesses can be made up for by God's grace and support. Perhaps you think you are not called to lead because you do not see yourself in a public role, always in the spotlight or busy with social activity. But leadership is not limited to certain roles. You can be a leader among the people around you, in your family, at work, and above all, a leader of your own life. Leadership can be applied in many areas. What matters is to be a leader who fills their life with meaning and success."],["Unusual leaders are those who do not fit the standard stereotypes of leadership, yet thanks to their unique traits and qualities are able to influence others effectively and achieve great results. Unusual leaders have their own strengths and their own challenges, and both are worth looking at.","Unusual leaders often take a non-standard approach to problems and tasks, which allows them to find new, unexpected solutions. That is also why they can meet scepticism and rejection of their unusual approaches from society or from part of their team.","The superhero of our book is Nehemiah. We began with his story, and we will keep discovering interesting facts about him. At first his duty was to serve wine to the king. It was a special and responsible task: he had to taste the wine before serving it so that the king would not be poisoned. So the king paid close attention to how his servant felt and behaved. If he noticed a change in his behaviour or that he seemed unwell, it made the king uneasy. Whether on purpose or not, Nehemiah used this to bring his request to the king.","«Wherefore the king said unto me, Why is thy countenance sad, seeing thou art not sick? this is nothing else but sorrow of heart. Then I was very sore afraid, and said unto the king, Let the king live for ever: why should not my countenance be sad, when the city, the place of my fathers' sepulchres, lieth waste, and the gates thereof are consumed with fire?»","This gave Nehemiah the chance to bring his request and a plan of action for rebuilding the walls of Jerusalem to the king.","One of the strengths of such leaders is the ability to see a situation from different angles and to find the best way to bring order to its different sides. They can break through the walls of conventional thinking and stereotypes, which helps them see solutions that others may miss.","Such leaders are usually open to new ideas and ready to experiment without fear of risk. Their unconventional approaches may surprise others or even raise doubts, but this is exactly what allows them to change the status quo and make progress. It is worth noting, though, that unusual approaches can lead to uncertainty or unpredictable results. So such leaders must be ready for challenges and able to adapt as the situation changes. It is also not always easy for them to build stable relationships with others, because their ideas can meet resistance or misunderstanding.","Especially when a problem is hard to solve or a stagnation hard to break, it is the unusual leaders who find a way. Their advantage is that they see differently from others. In reality such people often meet misunderstanding among those around them, and their ideas are rejected. So these leaders are constantly tempted to lose faith in their abilities and stop growing. There may be many mistakes and failed experiments in their experience, but it is worth understanding this: our weaknesses are the flip side of our strengths. Society always tries to fit personalities into a common mould, and unusual leaders adapt to avoid friction. Seeing yourself as a unique person and believing in your approach and vision can be the deciding factor for a breakthrough and success.","It takes no small courage to defend your uniqueness.","Courage plays an important role in leadership, especially when a leader faces challenges that concern their uniqueness, their idea or their approach.","Leaders often face criticism or rejection of ideas that differ from the accepted ones. Courage helps a leader not to let criticism undermine their confidence in the uniqueness of the idea, and to stay true to their convictions.","A leader may face opposition or negative reactions if their ideas or actions differ from the traditional ones. Courage makes it possible to defend your values and ideals regardless of the pressure around you. It helps a leader stay authentic and true to themselves, even when that means stepping outside accepted standards.","The otherness of unusual leaders can also affect how they communicate with others. This may come both from their difference from others and from the insecurity that arises because they do not see confirmation of their leadership qualities in themselves. It is important for unusual leaders to find a way to communicate effectively with different types of people and to convey their ideas clearly and persuasively.","For me personally, communication has always been hard. Every conversation demanded enormous effort from me. It was easier for me to connect with others at a distance than up close. Over time I noticed, and heard from friends, that my way of communicating, when it was hard for me to share my feelings and to understand other people's feelings and needs, gave the impression that I did not care much for people. Some took this trait of mine as pride and a sense of superiority. That troubled me deeply. A challenge stood before me: could I be an effective leader if I was not a good communicator? On the one hand, it was important to understand and accept that I, like every person, am unlike others, yet I can be a leader with my own unique way of influence. On the other hand, I set myself the task of learning communication skills. For that I had to decide to reach out to people even when I wanted to avoid it. Practice is the first rule in mastering any skill. This side of my personality became a priority for me for a long time. And although inside I remain the same person who finds strength and inspiration in solitude, I keep learning to communicate and I do it constantly.","Whatever personal qualities set you apart from the common image of a successful leader, they should not stop you from having a unique influence on your own life and the lives of others. The ways you differ from others are your personal challenge and, at the same time, your advantage.","Another unexpected challenge for a leader can be one of their strengths: being multi-talented. Yes, you read that right. I mean exceptionally gifted people who have a wide range of abilities and pick up new skills very quickly. The trap here can be the belief that everything they take on will bring some success. A feeling appears that what others achieve through discipline, hard study and work comes to them very easily. Such a leader may then face several problems. First, they also have a «multi-vision», that is, no clarity about which direction to go. So they become either superficial in many fields or inconsistent in all of them. Second, they do not give enough time to growth. To them, leadership looks like ninety-nine percent talent and one percent work. In practice it is the other way round: those who become successful and influential leaders are the ones who see leadership as ninety-nine percent work and only one percent natural ability.","I know many cases where talented, intelligent and charismatic people remained talented, promising and charismatic, but only for themselves. And on the other hand, many successful and influential people did not stand out for any special charisma, yet through hard work they achieved the most."],["Confidence is an important part of a leader's effectiveness. Insecurity, on the other hand, can be a thief that limits our potential and keeps us from success. When we do not believe in ourselves and our abilities, it can lead to consequences like these:","Limited goals. Insecurity can make us set our goals very low or not set them at all, because we do not believe we can reach them.","Avoiding challenges. Insecurity can lead us to avoid new challenges and opportunities because we are afraid we will not cope or that we will fail.","Lost opportunities. Insecurity can keep us from taking the initiative or sharing our ideas, and this can cost us important opportunities.","Less influence on others. Insecurity can reduce your influence on your team or the people you lead, because people will sense your hesitation and uncertainty.","Stress and anxiety. Insecurity can raise our levels of stress and anxiety, because we constantly doubt our actions and decisions.","But it is important to remember that insecurity can be overcome. It is a process of self-improvement and growth, in which it matters to work on your self-esteem and build confidence in yourself.","Were all great leaders confident from birth, free of any doubt about their abilities? When we watch outstanding leaders, it may seem that the feeling of doubt is unknown to them. They always make bold decisions and are sure of themselves. But in reality, confident leaders are not those who have no doubts but those who overcome them with bold decisions. Picture Nehemiah, who took on the enormous challenge of leading the people of Jerusalem to rebuild the walls. He had to overcome many doubts within himself. He had to leave his position and risk going to people who were neither materially nor emotionally ready to embrace the idea of restoring a ruined city. On top of that, Jerusalem was surrounded by other peoples who were hostile to the Jews and set on preventing its walls from rising again. In such an environment it is very hard to rely on support from outside; a leader must have firm confidence to withstand great opposition. If you know the Bible story of Nehemiah, you will remember that the first thing he faced was not threats. People began to mock him and jeer at whether he could accomplish what he had set out to do.","«But when Sanballat the Horonite, and Tobiah the servant, the Ammonite, and Geshem the Arabian, heard it, they laughed us to scorn, and despised us, and said, What is this thing that ye do? will ye rebel against the king?» Nehemiah 2:19.","«Now Tobiah the Ammonite was by him, and he said, Even that which they build, if a fox go up, he shall even break down their stone wall.» Nehemiah 4:3.","Do not expect everyone to support or accept your leadership. There will always be people, especially at the start of your journey when there are no results yet, only intentions, who will question you as a leader. You cannot prevent others from judging you negatively; the only thing you can influence is yourself. Your success depends on your decisions, not on other people's opinions. The proof will be the result of your work, not what people thought of you at the beginning. So focus not on what those who do not believe in you might say, but on your work and its results.","What sets a confident leader apart from an insecure one is that the confident leader does what the insecure one only thinks about doing, even though both have similar feelings. So it is decision, and decision alone, that turns an ordinary person into a leader. Confidence is gained through constant decisions. Nothing can replace your confidence: not your intelligence, not your talent, not your charisma. Confidence is the energy that lights up all your qualities and abilities. It is like the electricity that gives light and makes every appliance in your home work. Without power, nothing in your home will work. It is better to make mistakes than to lose your confidence by constantly worrying about how you will look in other people's eyes.","I remember my first experience of preaching. Today I can laugh about it, but back then it was not funny at all. I was asked to speak at a Sunday church service. I prepared for long hours, and with every day that brought my turn closer, I felt as if I were walking to my punishment. My notes were full of Bible quotations and a pile of thoughts I had carefully written down. I was ready to amaze everyone with the depth of my message and touch hearts with a fiery speech. Why not? Let them know what a living sermon is, and what a spiritual giant is in their midst. It took me five to seven minutes to get through all my notes, which weighed more than the Bible itself. When I stopped in complete confusion, the people never did work out what that had been, an introduction or a warm-up. A heavy silence fell; I felt that everyone could hear my heart pounding. Those minutes of silence lasted an eternity, and I did not know what to do next. Afterwards, sitting with a friend over coffee, I said just one thing: «Never in my life, do you hear me, never will I go up there again to disgrace myself like that.» But time passed, and once again I had to preach at a church service. I do not remember how I agreed to it, but when the moment came for me to go up, my legs felt like lead and I could not stand. Then the pastor in charge of the service came over and asked me: «Why are you still sitting?» I answered: «I can't go up, I'll fail.» And then he said a sentence that became historic for me: «If you don't go up now, you never will! Even if you forget every word and say only one word, ‘Amen’, it will be a personal victory for you.» He inspired me to make the decision and overcome my insecurity. Even if my sermon could not be called a success, the main thing I had to do was to defeat my timidity.","The main thing I learned in fighting insecurity was to free myself from wanting to please people and win their approval. The main thing for every leader is to focus on their task. To think not about how people rate me but about how effectively I am reaching my goal. Take a preacher as an example: if, standing at the pulpit, you aim even subconsciously to please your listeners, the result will be disappointment either way. Every time I stand before people, I remind myself: «I am here only to bring my message to people. My goal is their well-being and success.» When a doctor treats a patient, what matters to him is the person, not the impression he makes on them.","Do not waste time building up the confidence that people like you. Focus on your mission, not on yourself. Free yourself from the desire to please others and turn your attention to the task. Better to be than to seem. Seeking glory from people and serving a great calling are two things that do not go together.","«How can ye believe, which receive honour one of another, and seek not the honour that cometh from God only?» John 5:44.","«For do I now persuade men, or God? or do I seek to please men? for if I yet pleased men, I should not be the servant of Christ.» Galatians 1:10.","Your confidence rests on your mission and on the gifts that can serve others. Your desire is to change this world for the better and to make your contribution to the salvation and growth of others. Your work is the measure of your leadership and your values. So the conclusion is this: confidence is a matter not of self-suggestion but of values and priorities."],["Understanding the limits of your abilities is an important part of growing both as a leader and as a person. It helps us be objective about our capabilities and avoid overestimating ourselves, which can lead to unproductive situations or failure. Remember that every person has limits and weaknesses. Accept yourself as you are and strive to develop your potential, whatever the circumstances.","Understanding the limits of our abilities helps us to be more objective, to strive for growth and improvement, and to spend ourselves on what is truly valuable and needed.","A realistic assessment of your abilities, weaknesses and strengths is essential for success as a leader. But there are two very common mistakes here. The first: we believe we are right about everything because we can handle everything on our own, our judgement is always correct, and we understand ourselves and others well. The second: we believe our shortcomings and limited abilities make success impossible, and this becomes an excuse for our failures. These false judgements become obstacles to growth as a leader and as a person. In the first case we consider ourselves perfect and see no need to change; in the second we consider ourselves born losers who cannot change.","The path of leadership is always a path of transformation, improvement and growth throughout life. The main problem with both false judgements is that there is no process of change. For a leader, the main work is work on yourself; everything else is the result of that work. All the achievements and problems that come up along the way are a reflection of the leader's inner world. This is especially true when the same scenarios repeat at different times, in different circumstances and with different people. They are a mirror of something that is part of the leader. If something like this happens and the situation repeats again and again, it is high time to think about the cause. All successes and problems are born inside the leader. Well, almost all. Let us look at common mistakes and reactions to problems; what they have in common is that the situation repeats like a carbon copy, only in a different context.","Imagine a person whose life keeps producing similar situations along a similar script, whether at work, in relationships or in dealing with others. In the first case the person constantly blames circumstances and shifts responsibility onto others. They sincerely believe they are only the object of what happens, not the subject who may have helped create the conditions for these problems. Such a person will always see themselves as a victim of circumstances and of people who abused their trust. That may be partly true, but if such situations keep repeating, then an inner script is being replayed inside the leader, and this has to be admitted in order to change how they see the problem. As I said, almost everything that happens around us is merely a reflection of what is inside the leader. That is why the position of blame and victimhood is neither constructive nor effective.","In the second case the person is aware of their shortcomings and limits but goes no further towards change. Instead they find a simple answer to everything: «That's just who I am, and I can't do anything about it.» They take no responsibility for the causes of their problems, pointing to their natural weaknesses and flaws. After all, if that is who they are, how can it be their fault? This can be a very convenient defensive tactic, but it is a very poor strategy for growth.","One of my favourite verses in the Bible is:","If we truly want to change our lives, we have to tear down all the protective walls that hide the real cause of our problems. And that cause is mostly inside us, not in other people or outside circumstances. This really does take a sincere and strong desire. If our desire to change our life is immature, we will look for change in other people or dream that the circumstances around us will change. When a person is thirsty, they have a strong physical need for water; every cell of their body demands it. Everything inside is aimed at satisfying that need. They will not deceive themselves by saying it is enough to point out that other people have water. Everything in them is focused on finding relief, and, importantly, right now. If we approach the search for truth inside ourselves in the same way, the whole truth will open up to us, a truth able to fill us with a life of transformation and effectiveness. Like water for the body, this truth will become the source of our future success and flourishing.","Truth is a tool we should use for our inner enrichment and growth. So let us get rid of the leftovers of the old life in the form of these two common mental mistakes. If we have wrongly believed that the whole world was to blame for our failures, we can change our attitude, take responsibility and act as people who shape their own destiny through their decisions and actions. In the other case, we will stop excusing our weaknesses and start working on changing our character.","The key is to realise that all our character traits, our habits and our way of seeing the world were once formed by upbringing, experience and the information that came to our attention. All of this built in us a certain pattern of behaviour and a way of acting in different circumstances. If the result does not satisfy us, we need to change the rules and rethink how we see the world and ourselves. It may be a hard road, but it is necessary if we want to see our lives change for the better. We are able to look inside ourselves, review all our settings and beliefs and change them. Most of what makes up our worldview was instilled over the course of our lives, so it is not a constant that cannot be changed. We are who we are not because that is who we truly are, but because we have shaped ourselves that way.","For me personally, the hardest thing was not the desire to change for the better, and not even the change itself. The hardest thing was to see the need for change and to realise exactly where and in what I needed to change. I always joke to myself: «If a bear in a circus can be taught to ride a bicycle, why can't I teach myself to do what I can't do yet?» Seriously, though, my rule is this: do not do what I feel like doing; do what I want to get done. And although I understand that not everything depends on me, my reaction to events and situations does depend on me. So in any case, the responsibility for my attitude to events lies with me.","In truth, you have not yet discovered the limits of your abilities, nor imagined everything your potential makes possible. Most of the time our experience is only the experience of what we have always been used to doing. It is like a hall of mirrors where one object standing in the middle is reflected from every side, only at different angles. The mirrors themselves are neutral in this sense; they will show whatever you put there. It is not the mirrors that create the object; the object creates the image. So our circumstances are only a projection of what we hold inside: change the object and the image will change. Taking a step into something new means discovering new possibilities and new traits in yourself. And finally, a little joke:","After an operation to remove his appendix, a patient asks the doctor:","«Tell me, will I be able to play the violin after this?»","«Of course you will!»","«Strange. I couldn't before.»"],["Defining your own values is fundamental to personal growth and success, including in leadership. Values help us understand ourselves, our beliefs and our purpose in life better, and they shape our decisions and actions. Self-knowledge allows us to be active agents in our own lives instead of simply reacting to outside circumstances. It helps us set goals, choose priorities and solve important tasks. Knowing our values helps us understand where we want to grow and who we want to become. It spurs us on towards constant self-improvement. When we understand our values and beliefs, it is easier to lead others and inspire them towards shared goals. Defining our values helps us be consistent in our actions and in how we deal with others.","Defining your values is one of the most essential parts of leadership. Without it, leadership is impossible altogether. A leader is a person in the service of their values. This matters so much that a leader's other qualities, their charisma and talents, mean nothing if the leader is not aware of their mission. The question «For what and for whom am I doing this?» is fundamental. There is an old parable that shows how people can do the same work yet hold different values:","Three men were working on the construction of a temple. During a break someone came up to the first worker and asked: «What are you doing here?»","The first worker answered: «I'm working, and I get paid for it. I'm just doing my job, like a thousand times before.»","Then the second worker came over and heard the question. He answered with a smile: «I'm building a beautiful building. I lay the stones with care so that it looks beautiful and serves people.»","The third worker heard the question during his break and answered with a sparkle in his eyes: «I'm building a temple for the Lord. Every stone, every brick, every detail is given for the glory of God. This temple will be a place where people can find shelter and inspiration and grow in their faith.»","Values determine the reward. What becomes of these three once the work is done? Most likely the first, having been paid for his hours, will be unhappy with his wages. People usually think they have been paid too little and deserve more. Either way, money is the whole reward he received for his work. The second probably received more than money: he will be proud to have had a part in building a beautiful building, and he can count on people's praise. The third had different values. He built a Temple for God, and his reward goes beyond wages and human recognition. Every time human hearts turn to God in that Temple, he has a share in it. His reward is eternal.","«Take heed that ye do not your alms before men, to be seen of them: otherwise ye have no reward of your Father which is in heaven. Therefore when thou doest thine alms, do not sound a trumpet before thee, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and in the streets, that they may have glory of men. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.","But when thou doest alms, let not thy left hand know what thy right hand doeth:","That thine alms may be in secret: and thy Father which seeth in secret himself shall reward thee openly.» Matthew 6:1–4.","What reward do you want from your work? If we do not know our values, it can lead to dissatisfaction or even disappointment with leadership. If we expect recognition and reward from people, that is the shortest road to disappointment. People can be ungrateful, quickly forget everything you have done for them, and perhaps even become your enemies. Believe me, we all have that experience. Many times the fiercest enemies in my life were not people I had wronged but people from whom I deserved gratitude and respect. If my values had rested on expecting recognition from people, it would have destroyed me as a leader at the very start. People's gratitude matters to each of us, but even without it we understand our values and know for Whom we do what we do.","Finding your reward in yourself, in your own work, can bring joy only for a while, and may then turn into dissatisfaction. An emptiness can open up in your soul when your contribution is quickly forgotten and not valued by those who enjoy the fruit of your labour. There is the feeling of not being recognised, of your part in the common cause being underrated. It is very easy to become a person who feels passed over and unneeded, and to slip into the role of a victim.","Only an awareness of our true values turns us into unbreakable winners who receive their reward no matter what: even if the pay did not match the labour, even if people looking at the Temple never remember your name. The reward comes from the One who «seeth in secret» and «shall reward thee openly». Nothing gives as much joy from work done as eternal values.","Defining our values helps us understand what motivates and inspires us. It lets us understand our goals better and reach them. In any activity we need inspiration and energy. But like everyone else, we sometimes lose the motivation to do things. This is not only a matter of simple physical and emotional fatigue; above all it is a matter of values. It is values that give us the strength to get up every day and do what we do, to pay the price for our convictions. Values give us physical, emotional and spiritual energy. Conversely, the absence of real values leads to quick burnout and exhaustion.","People have sometimes asked me: who or what drives you to work if there is no boss or mentor over you checking your time and your work? I don't need anyone to remind me now and then what my duties are, or a shoulder to cry on. My boss and my manager are my mission and my values. What I do, I do for the sake of what I believe in.","In the story of Nehemiah there is a moment when everyone working on the walls grew tired and had no strength or inspiration to go on. It is a familiar situation in any team. But Nehemiah was a man who knew his values and why he was taking part in rebuilding the walls of Jerusalem. So in his speech to the people he touched on the most important thing of all: the question of values.","«And Judah said, The strength of the bearers of burdens is decayed, and there is much rubbish; so that we are not able to build the wall.» Nehemiah 4:10.","«Remember the Lord, which is great and terrible, and fight for your brethren, your sons, and your daughters, your wives, and your houses.» Nehemiah 4:14.","When we understand our values and beliefs, it is easier to lead others and inspire them to reach shared goals. Defining our values helps us be leaders in our actions and in how we relate to others.","Most people need someone who can inspire and support them when they lack motivation. There is nothing wrong or strange about that. We should understand our role in the group and not ignore the needs of others. Each of us, however motivated, needs the support of others.","I am grateful to my family, my friends, my church and my teachers, who inspire and support me and stand by my side. This gives me confidence that we can overcome every obstacle on the way to our goals, and it creates a unique synergy of mutual support.","Knowing our values helps us understand where we want to grow and who we want to become. It spurs us on to constant self-improvement. It is hard to work on yourself if you do not understand why you are doing it and what reward your effort will bring. Values create powerful motivation for change. Our values shape us. The apostle Paul says:","«Know ye not that they which run in a race run all, but one receiveth the prize? So run, that ye may obtain.","And every man that striveth for the mastery is temperate in all things. Now they do it to obtain a corruptible crown; but we an incorruptible.","I therefore so run, not as uncertainly; so fight I, not as one that beateth the air:","But I keep under my body, and bring it into subjection: lest that by any means, when I have preached to others, I myself should be a castaway.» 1 Corinthians 9:24–27.","Often the reason a person cannot overcome laziness or bad habits is not a lack of willpower but a lack of understanding why it is needed. And that depends directly on understanding values. If a person realises «why this is necessary», they will find the strength and the way «how to do it».","When we clearly understand our values, it is easier to make decisions in situations where values clash or a hard choice has to be made. Then our values become a navigation compass for our lives. They help us make decisions that fit our true nature and purpose. When we face difficult situations or moral dilemmas, our values serve as a pattern that helps us decide what really matters to us.","Values can help us focus on what truly matters in our lives and set aside needless deliberation and the pull of outside factors. When we know what we value most, it becomes easier to make choices that let us live by our principles and stay true to ourselves.","Values also help us set priorities in life. When we know what really matters to us, we can focus on what helps us grow and reach our goals, and turn down what might hinder our growth and success.","Values also help us build strong relationships with other people, especially those who share our values. They help us find common ground with others and lay a foundation for mutual understanding and support.","So understanding our values is an important step in self-knowledge and personal growth. It helps us live more consciously and with more focus, in line with our true convictions, and that is a key factor in success and fulfilment in life.","Focusing on our values helps us concentrate on what really matters and avoid spending energy on unimportant things. It helps us conserve energy and not scatter our attention on trivial or unreachable goals. When we clearly understand what is truly important to us, we can direct our efforts, time and resources towards those goals.","Focusing on our values helps us make important choices in life. It helps us see which areas of life matter most to us and avoid imbalance, where we are so immersed in one area that the others suffer.","Values act as a filter that helps us sift out what is unnecessary and unimportant. We can focus more on the goals and tasks that match our values and avoid spending time on what will not bring us real satisfaction or success.","Focusing on our values also helps us maintain and strengthen our motivation. When we do what matches our values, it inspires us and gives meaning to our work. We become more engaged and enjoy what we do more.","So focusing on our values helps us find our way in life and preserve our energy, motivation and the joy of reaching our goals. It lets us live more consciously and make balanced decisions that bring joy and success into our lives.","And finally, a joke as a bonus for your patience and attention:","A man woke up early one morning and started getting ready. His wife asked in surprise: «Darling, where are you off to so early?» He smiled and said: «My love, I heard a wonderful proverb: the early bird catches the worm. And I want to make the most of that gift.»","Taking his wallet, he hurried out of the house. Some time later he appeared at the door with a black eye and no wallet. His wife asked anxiously: «What happened, dear?» Still smiling, he said: «Darling, it seems someone got up even earlier than I did.»","The most motivated leaders do the best work."],["This is a key question that faces every leader all the time. A leader is always confronted with challenges, but how they approach them determines how successful their leadership will be. Leadership means responsibility, defining your goal and striving to reach it despite challenges and obstacles. So a leader's answer to a challenge is to accept it, respond to it and act to reach the goal.","A leader's approach to challenges really does determine their success in the role. Leadership requires a readiness to meet difficulties, take risks and make hard decisions. Yet it is precisely the response to these challenges that allows a leader to grow, develop and become stronger.","A leader must be ready for the unexpected, solve problems and learn from mistakes. Every challenge a leader faces is an opportunity to show their leadership qualities, their creativity and their ability to act amid uncertainty.","It is important for a leader to see challenges not as obstacles but as opportunities for growth and improvement. Answering a challenge may require innovative approaches, the ability to mobilise a team, the skill of making hard decisions and confidence in one's own actions.","Leadership is about taking an active stance and having confidence in yourself. Challenges can test a leader's qualities, but the right approach to them helps a leader grow and become stronger in the role.","So a leader who is ready to answer challenges has the chance to achieve great results and inspire others by example. Answering challenges is an important part of a leader's growth, strengthening their leadership qualities and helping them succeed in many areas of life.","Leadership is a demanding role, and certain factors can keep a leader from making decisions.","Insecurity. A leader may doubt their abilities and their capacity to make the right decisions. This may stem from uncertainty about their knowledge, experience or skills. In that case the leader puts off the decision and drags the process out. Of course a leader needs time to weigh and think everything through before deciding or speaking. But if they do not do it in time, it weakens both their self-confidence and their position as a leader in the eyes of others. Indecision and delay are poor counsellors for any leader. On the other hand, if a leader can make decisions firmly and confidently, it shows their inner conviction and faith in the success of their cause.","The Bible story of David and Goliath clearly shows how different leaders behaved. For forty days Goliath came out before the army of Israel and its king, who was in fact the leader of the people. But in all that time the king could not make any decision at all about what to do with Goliath and his army. The real leader turned out to be David, who, on hearing Goliath's threats, immediately decided to face him in single combat.","«And David spake to the men that stood by him, saying, What shall be done to the man that killeth this Philistine, and taketh away the reproach from Israel? for who is this uncircumcised Philistine, that he should defy the armies of the living God?» 1 Samuel 17:26.","That was a decision worthy of a true leader. What is more, it seems David worked out along the way how exactly he would fight Goliath, who outmatched him in strength, experience and weapons. The main thing here is that David answered the challenge. The king of Israel, meanwhile, could not bring himself to make any decision for forty days. The longer he hesitated, the harder it was for him to decide.","From my own experience I can say that it is sometimes better to make a decision that may turn out to be wrong than to show yourself as someone unable to decide. Fear of making a mistake can become an obstacle to decisions. This happens because we always see only part of the picture and cannot predict the consequences of a decision with one hundred percent certainty, so we put it off, since none of the options is ideal. There is always a risk that the decision will prove wrong, but that only becomes clear afterwards. This difficult dilemma always faces a leader. At the same time, a leader understands that even the most correct decision, if made too late, is already the wrong one.","We know of no leader who never made a wrong decision, but we know of no leader who made no decisions at all.","Fear of responsibility. The role of a leader carries responsibility, and some leaders may be afraid to bear such a weight and the consequences of their decisions. This is the other side of leadership. Responsibility can cause discomfort and a wish to avoid it by any means. But leadership does not exist outside of responsibility. We have to accept it as a given and learn to handle it with balance. Responsibility concerns not only the results of decisions, which we have already discussed, but also the moral and emotional state of the leader and of those they lead. A leader is not only someone who makes decisions but someone who inspires by example. Even if a leader makes a mistake, it is not fatal if they can keep their composure and admit that they are human like everyone else and, to a degree, entitled to make mistakes. What matters is not only whether the leader erred but how they respond and act afterwards. A leader can always count on understanding and support if they act in the interests of their community. People can forgive a leader many mistakes if they are sure the leader takes responsibility and cares about their progress. On the other hand, if the leader's position is unclear and they seem indifferent to other people's future, even a small mistake can weaken their authority. The words of the Gospel apply here: «her sins, which are many, are forgiven; for she loved much». For a leader, this means that one who loves and holds their position for the good of others has a great deal of trust in reserve, mistakes notwithstanding. And a leader in whom people do not see someone who cares about them will find far less support.","Fear of conflict. A leader may want to avoid decisions that could cause conflict or opposition. A dilemma may arise when the leader realises that no option can meet everyone's expectations. Seeking a compromise can narrow the gap between different opinions, but a leader must consciously make decisions in line with their mission and for the good of all. We have to accept that it is hard, and sometimes impossible, for a leader to please everyone. Only a sincere and open position can convince others that the leader is acting in everyone's interest.","For a leader, giving in means avoiding or refusing a challenge, and that can mean missing a chance to develop and grow. Every challenge holds potential for a leader's growth and a path for their progress.","Personally, I have often found decision-making hard. On the one hand you understand that every option contains something unknown, that you cannot foresee all the risks and consequences. On the other hand, not deciding is already the worst scenario. Taking everything in and foreseeing everyone's reaction is very hard. So a leader has to learn to act with limited information and time. Even with time it is not always possible to tell whether a decision was right or whether a better option existed, because we can only judge the outcome of the other choice hypothetically. But I can say with confidence that many problems arose because no decisions were made when circumstances demanded them, when decisions were postponed to avoid opposition or a possible mistake. A situation that calls for a decision tends to grow into an even bigger problem, and potential opposition tends to turn into open conflict. The absence of a decision is a position of weakness, and weakness always gives rise to a force that wants to exploit it. It is like a vacuum: if you do not fill it, outside forces will certainly fill it, and they can be destructive. Even if it turns out you did not choose the best option, at least you kept your position as a leader able to take a stand. You can learn from mistakes; you cannot learn when you do nothing.","«The story of the Leader and the Desert:","Long, long ago, in a faraway land, there lived a tribal chief named Abdel. He was a wise and just leader who always cared for the well-being of his tribe. One day, when the tribe was facing severe trials, Abdel had to make an extremely important decision.","On a scorching summer day the spring from which the tribe drew its water suddenly dried up because of a long drought. The tribe was in a desperate state, and Abdel understood that without water they faced death. Councils were held, but no one found a solution.","Then Abdel made a hard decision: he resolved to leave his tribe and set out on a long journey across the desert to find a new source of water. It was a dangerous journey, but Abdel was ready to sacrifice his comfort and safety to save his people.","For Abdel's tribe, things began to change. At first they felt helpless and abandoned. But over time, when the water ran out completely, they realised that nothing would change if they stayed passive. Pressed by their situation, they began to pull together, search for other sources of water and even learn to collect the morning dew.","After long and dangerous days of walking through the desert, Abdel found a spring. His heart filled with joy, but he was far from his tribe. Abdel returned, bringing news of the new spring, which became the source of new life for his tribe.","Abdel's leadership showed that sometimes a decision demands great sacrifice and stepping beyond comfort. He did not give in to circumstances; instead he answered the challenge and acted for the good of his tribe. His decision saved lives and changed the way his tribe approached the problem of water.»","Yes, in a time of trial each of us faces a dilemma: how to respond to circumstances that may be unpredictable and difficult. Some people find an excuse to give in to circumstances and stop acting, believing they cannot influence the situation. Others, the leaders, answer the challenge by making decisions and taking responsibility for their actions, even in hard circumstances.","Leaders understand that they can influence their surroundings and overcome obstacles. They believe in their abilities and focus on finding creative and effective ways to solve problems. Taking responsibility means carrying the weight of decisions and their consequences, which can be heavy, but it helps a leader grow and develop. By overcoming inner doubts and fears, leaders become an example for others and bring positive change to their teams, organisations and society. Do not be afraid of mistakes; every leader makes them, and sadly there is no avoiding it. What you should really fear is being a leader who cannot act or make decisions, a leader without a clear position and vision of the future. I can imagine a leader who is imperfect and whose decisions are sometimes wrong, but I cannot imagine a single leader who takes a passive stance and makes no decisions.","And finally, our traditional joke corner:","At the international congress of pessimists, they resolved never to hold another congress.","There is no leader who makes perfect decisions, just as there is no such thing as a leader who makes none."],["Fear of the unknown always brings tension, hesitation and indecision. It is a natural human reaction to the uncertainty and unfamiliarity of new situations. But must the fear of the unknown always hold back our actions and our relationships with the world around us?","Leadership is the ability to guide others, take responsibility for decisions and bring about positive change. To become a successful leader, we have to change our thinking and let go of the fear of the unknown.","Instead of seeing the unknown as a threat, let us see it as an opportunity for growth and development. Every great leader faced the unknown and felt fear, but they did not let it stop them. They moved forward with conviction, were ready to take risks and learned from their mistakes.","Remember that the unknown is a chance to discover new opportunities, meet new people and unlock your potential. If we let fear of the unknown hold back our actions, we will never truly grow or fulfil our dreams.","Letting go of the fear of the unknown is the first step to becoming a true leader, one who is ready to take responsibility and act even in unfamiliar situations. Set yourself the task of overcoming fear, move forward with confidence and act with an open heart and mind.","Change your thinking: let go of the fear of the unknown and give yourself the chance to grow, develop and become a true leader of your own life's road. And remember, the greatest victories await those who have the courage to step into the unknown and open up new horizons.","«So I came to Jerusalem, and was there three days. And I arose in the night, I and some few men with me; neither told I any man what my God had put in my heart to do at Jerusalem.» Nehemiah 2:11–12.","Nehemiah faced an important choice: to stay in a comfortable and influential post at the king's court, or to take a risk and step into the unknown to help his fellow countrymen. He chose the latter. Stepping into the unknown, he asked King Artaxerxes for permission to go up to Jerusalem.","It was a great test for Nehemiah. He was living in a foreign land and did not know what awaited him in Jerusalem. He would face great difficulties: rebuilding the city and its walls, standing against enemies and the distrust of the local people. But with a strong call in his heart, Nehemiah gathered his will and courage and went into the unknown.","Through his persistence, courage and faith, Nehemiah became an unusual leader who inspired people and drew them together, and together they rebuilt the walls of Jerusalem in record time. Nehemiah showed that a readiness to go into the unknown, trusting an inner call, can turn an ordinary person into an outstanding leader able to accomplish the impossible for a shared goal.","New situations and tasks. When a leader faces new situations or tasks that require unusual solutions, they may feel uncertainty and fear of the unknown. Yet at the same time these new challenges can be a source of growth, both personal and professional. A true leader knows how to handle these feelings and turn the unknown into an advantage, drawing on their knowledge, experience and understanding of the situation.","For me, being a leader is a constant journey into the unknown. Constant change and movement become a new form of stability. The one thing I have learned in all this time is that the only constant is that everything keeps changing, and that a leader has the right to choose in everything except the right to choose to have no choice.","Society and the world around us are always changing, and an important task is to stay open to everything new. I have always enjoyed starting new projects, learning new skills and taking on new tasks. We were not ready for every project we undertook. We often faced hard problems: finding material resources, a lack of experience and information. But I have learned that if you are ready for change and have enough motivation, the unknown can be turned into new discoveries and success. Even the hardest tasks get solved once you start working on them. A new task may look impossible. But if you approach it on the principle of «eating an elephant one small bite at a time», step by step the unknown becomes clear and conquered.","Working with different people. A leader who leads a team or an organisation often faces the challenge of working with different people who have different characters, values and styles of work. Handling the unknown in dealing with new colleagues or team members may require a leader to adapt and build an effective connection with each person.","It is very important to have the skills to connect and work with new people, to bring them into new projects and to create an atmosphere of cooperation and shared interest in success. At its heart, every task and project is teamwork, the interaction of different people with different skills and professions. Joined together, they can give birth to something new and unique that none of them could do alone.","These may be people from outside your usual circle: of different ages and worldviews, sometimes very different from each other. What matters is understanding their values and respecting their worldview and convictions. For me, every person is a teacher, whatever their age, education or views. There is always something you can and should learn from them.","Many times I have found myself among very different, even opposite, kinds of people: politicians, businesspeople, religious figures, artists, even criminal (or formerly criminal) personalities, «underground» youth and many others. These are completely different worlds, values and cultures. Add different nationalities and traditions, and you get a small picture of the world around us.","The apostle Paul, who constantly faced the unknown in circumstances and among people, wrote:","«For though I be free from all men, yet have I made myself servant unto all, that I might gain the more.","And unto the Jews I became as a Jew, that I might gain the Jews; to them that are under the law, as under the law, that I might gain them that are under the law;","To them that are without law, as without law, (being not without law to God, but under the law to Christ,) that I might gain them that are without law.","To the weak became I as weak, that I might gain the weak: I am made all things to all men, that I might by all means save some.","And this I do for the gospel's sake, that I might be partaker thereof with you.» 1 Corinthians 9:19–23.","Taking risks. A leader who wants to reach new heights often has to take risks. Entering new markets, expanding a business or introducing innovations can involve the unknown and uncertainty. But a successful leader knows how to weigh the risks and make balanced decisions, which allows them to succeed even amid uncertainty. I will go further: a leader who is not ready to take risks and is set only on preserving what has been achieved is already beginning to lose influence and is stagnating. The only way to keep what you have is to be ready to risk it for something new.","«He that gathereth not with me scattereth.» Luke 11:23.","Yes, sometimes the only way to keep what you have, or to reach new goals, is to take a risk and accept the challenge of something new. Avoiding risk can lead to stagnation, lack of growth and lost opportunities. The ability to take risks and leave your comfort zone is essential for growth, development and success.","Remember the Bible parable of the talents in the Gospel of Matthew 25:14–30, which Jesus told His followers.","In this story, a rich man gave his talents to his servants before going on a journey. One received five talents, another two, and the third one. The first and second servants took a risk and invested their talents, and they doubled them. But the third servant was afraid and decided to bury his talent in the ground to keep it safe.","When the master returned, he called his servants to account. The first servant reported that he had gained five more talents with his five, the second that he had gained two more with his two. The master praised them and made them partners in his affairs. But the third servant came and said that he had been afraid and had buried his talent in the ground. The master was angry with him, took his talent away and gave it to the one who had the most.","This story underlines how important it is to take risks and to use the gifts and abilities we have been given. Jesus taught that we should use our abilities wisely and responsibly, investing effort in building God's kingdom on earth. The talents in this parable symbolise God's gifts, which we are meant to develop and use to serve God and people. This approach to our talents brings true fulfilment and spiritual riches.","Unexpected events and crises. Leadership also faces the challenge of managing unpredictable events and crises. Running into unexpected problems or changes in outside conditions can force a leader to look for quick and effective solutions to keep things stable and successful.","I always say that life, like a clock, is ceaseless forward motion. Only three things make us change and move forward: enough motivation within us, outside factors, or a crisis. If we do not want to, or do not realise in time that we need to take risks and change, a crisis may come that leaves us no chance not to respond.","That is what happened in the story of the first church, among the apostles and disciples of Jesus. They had all been given the task to go and preach the Gospel throughout the world rather than staying in one place. They heard this call once, twice and many more times, but they still stayed in Jerusalem. Until persecution came. Then they scattered across the world, not only preaching but also working miracles. That is what happens when we try to hold on to our comfort zone.","It is important to note that a leader who faces the unknown can see it as an opportunity to develop and grow. The right approach to the challenges of the unknown helps a leader develop skills, gain experience and become stronger and more confident in their abilities."],["Crises can be a real field for unlocking and developing a leader's potential. A crisis demands quick decisions, creative thinking and the ability to work under pressure. It is crises that reveal leaders. Every famous leader we know of rose to prominence in the midst of crisis, in times of trial. A leader's potential is like a parachute: it opens only when it is used, and for that you have to jump. Sometimes the crisis itself, and our response to it, help us unlock potential that would never show itself in ordinary circumstances.","Challenges drive growth. A crisis demands that a leader step outside familiar scenarios and find new ways to solve problems. This drives development and the search for new skills, because the leader faces the question of what to do next and where to find new ways and new sources to sustain their projects. That is why we often hear: «When one door closes, another opens.» Perhaps the new doors were always open, and we simply had no need to look for them? Stagnation is a leader's chief enemy. A leader may stop growing if no new tasks arise that call for their involvement. A leader's place is always where there is a need for them and their involvement.","Discovering strengths. In a crisis, leaders are forced to use their strengths and unique abilities to overcome difficulties. This can unlock potential that may have been underused before. I think of the story of the founder of the Foursquare Church: she was a pastor of a church, but it was the crisis that confronted her that made her a world-famous leader.","Aimee Semple McPherson's story is the remarkable story of a woman who boldly stepped beyond tradition and became an outstanding leader despite many challenges and obstacles.","Born in 1890 in Canada, Aimee Semple showed remarkable courage and determination from a young age. Yet her path to leadership was far from easy. She was a divorced woman, which was quite unacceptable to the conservative society of the time. On top of that, Aimee wore make-up, which outraged church circles of the day.","But these circumstances did not stop Aimee. She became a pioneer of women's pastoral ministry and opened the way for women who dreamed of serving in the church. Even when some well-known denominations would not recognise her, Aimee did not lose her faith or confidence. On the contrary, this crisis pushed her to found her own denomination, the International Church of the Foursquare Gospel, which in time became one of the largest in the world.","Aimee Semple McPherson managed to use her unusual traits and to overcome the challenges and unbelief she met along the way. Her courage, faith and devotion helped her unlock her potential and become a great leader. She convincingly proved that being unconventional and brave can be real advantages for success in leadership.","But one day in 1926, while Aimee was resting on the California coast, something strange happened. She disappeared without a trace for several weeks. This caused panic among her followers and led to an intense search. Later Aimee turned up in Mexico, where she claimed she had been kidnapped.","This crisis became a great challenge for Aimee McPherson. She was subjected to sharp criticism and doubt from society and the press. But in spite of this, she answered the challenge with great resolve.","This event allowed her to show her strong will, courage and leadership qualities. She not only survived the crisis but managed to use it to strengthen her leadership. After the incident her popularity and influence only grew. Aimee Semple McPherson went on serving her followers, founding churches and doing charitable work.","The story of Aimee Semple McPherson is an example of how a leader can unlock their potential in the most unexpected and difficult circumstances. She not only came through the crisis but used it as an opportunity to grow and strengthen her influence as a leader.","Self-affirmation. Overcoming difficult situations and achieving success can raise our self-esteem and faith in our abilities as leaders. Nothing establishes us as leaders like overcoming hard tasks. The feeling we have after overcoming a challenge cannot be gained in any other way. For me, leadership is always an adrenaline rush that drives me to act. Personally, I don't need to go mountaineering or skydiving to feel something extraordinary. It is enough to start living by faith, to carry out projects despite every obstacle, to overcome challenges, and you get far more. Above all, it convinces you, despite every doubt, that you are able to lead and to influence the course of events. This is the practice you need to affirm yourself and strengthen your faith. It prepares you to be an even more confident leader, gaining new qualities and experience. Your story and experience will inspire and encourage others. You are not acting only for yourself; your victory matters not only to you but to the many people watching your story.","So crises can be an important tool for unlocking and developing a leader's potential, because it is crises that test a leader and reveal their true capabilities. Every challenge is an opportunity to grow, develop and show your true nature. The stature of a person is measured not only by their successes but by their ability to overcome difficulties and learn from their mistakes.","A leader is someone who has not only potential or charisma but also experience gained in times of crisis. There are qualities a leader can only gain in practice. And what matters most for a leader is how they respond to a crisis, how they behave in one situation or another. Seeing potential for growth in a crisis and turning it into success is the main trait of an experienced leader."],["Leadership always tests our resilience, demanding that we go beyond what is already known and boldly tackle what is unknown. This chapter is about the artistic dimension of leadership: the ability to exceed expectations, whatever the situation.","When we look at the leaders we know of, we often see their exploits and achievements, which seem almost unbelievable. But behind these exploits lies something more than talent or experience. It is faith in yourself and your own potential, the desire to keep moving forward despite every difficulty and uncertainty.","Leaders who exceed expectations are not afraid to try new ideas, act in unusual situations and take risks. They know how to find strength within themselves to overcome the fear of the unknown. They believe in themselves, believe in God's plan and in their ability to meet challenges, even when the road is unclear and hard.","This chapter reminds us that each of us has the potential to go beyond the known, overcome our own limits and move boldly forward. Leadership is not only a challenge but also an opportunity to influence the world around us and leave a mark on history.","The leader within us: finding inner motivation. Leadership involves the capacity for autonomy, but that does not mean being cut off from the team or refusing to cooperate. A true leader knows how to balance independence with the ability to cooperate and listen to others.","A leader's autonomy lies in being responsible for their decisions and actions without waiting for explanations or directives from others. A leader needs confidence in their abilities and the capacity to analyse a situation and define goals and the ways to reach them.","Yet this does not mean refusing advice, support and cooperation with the team. A leader's autonomy means the ability to solve problems independently and take responsibility for results, while being ready to listen to others' views and work with them.","Being aware of their own autonomy helps a leader set clear goals, make quick and well-founded decisions and use their resources effectively. It is the ability to lead a team to success, taking into account both their own needs and the team's.","A novice leader may be less autonomous, because they may lack experience and confidence. They may often turn to the team or to senior management for decisions and advice. They rely more on others' experience because they lack their own. This is normal while a leader is building up their own capital of skills.","When I became a pastor, my experience was zero. I found it hard to settle on a style and method for leading the church. So I chose to imitate what other leaders did and preached. I even chose the colour of my tie to match the leader I was trying to imitate. It may look funny now, but it helped me at a time when I had no experience and no clear sense of my own path.","As a leader gains experience and develops their own skills, they can become more autonomous. They learn to take responsibility for decisions and actions, though they may still waver in planning. Over time I began to feel my own experience taking shape, and a vision of my personal message as a leader. I began introducing my own programmes and became more independent.","A leader who has already gained considerable experience and the trust of their team can be highly autonomous. They are ready to take responsibility for important decisions, able to work independently and carry out their own strategies. Such a leader is now a person who understands their own path and carries out their vision. This is what we call a true leader: someone with a clear position who exerts influence through their gifting. Such a leader achieves great effectiveness. An experienced leader already has great influence. But the question remains: is there a path for further growth?","An outstanding leader has deep experience and unrivalled expertise and may have a high level of autonomy. They handle even the most difficult situations freely, have their own view on strategic questions and are able to make important decisions. This is the leader who becomes a top-tier leader. Only a few choose this level. Why choose? Because there is a price for such leadership. It is a privilege and a cross at the same time. That is why most leaders with the potential to become outstanding prefer to stay in a more comfortable place, at the level of an experienced leader. An outstanding leader pays a certain price for their position and influence. Going through all these challenges can be hard, but it can also open opportunities for personal and professional growth. Here are just a few reasons why.","An outstanding leader carries great responsibility to the team, the organisation and often the public. They must make important decisions that may affect many people. Responsibility is the main burden of leadership. Many people will link their successes and failures to this leader's decisions. They belong to themselves less than anyone else on the team. Not only the successes but also the blame for failures will be laid at the door of their leadership.","A leader invests a great deal of time and energy in work and growth. They may give many hours to planning, analysis, decision-making and developing skills. As I said before, they belong to themselves less than anyone else on the team, and that includes their time. An outstanding leader has no fixed working hours. They are always working, even on holiday, because responsibility does not lift from them even in their sleep. They must stay connected to their position at all times, not only outwardly in day-to-day operations but also inwardly, constantly growing.","«Meditate upon these things; give thyself wholly to them; that thy profiting may appear to all.","Take heed unto thyself, and unto the doctrine; continue in them: for in doing this thou shalt both save thyself, and them that hear thee.» 1 Timothy 4:15–16.","Ask me when my day off is, when I can completely free my mind from work and lift the responsibility from my heart, and we will hug each other and laugh together.","The high expectations placed on an outstanding leader can bring stress and psychological pressure. Results and excellence are expected of them. No account is taken of the fact that they remain an ordinary person like everyone else. Yet the attitude towards them and the demands on them will always be special.","An outstanding leader may often give up personal time, family gatherings or other pleasures to invest themselves in their work and improve their skills. It is a serious challenge for them to find a balance between work duties and devotion to family and loved ones. It is vital to protect yourself and your family, and to remember that you are responsible first of all to your family. Even so, there is a certain price an outstanding leader pays.","Outstanding leaders often come under criticism and face difficult challenges. They must be ready to meet hard situations and look for constructive solutions. Oh, here I could be the champion for the amount of criticism aimed at me. Not only a leader's mistakes or imperfections become targets of criticism, but even things the leader had nothing to do with. This happens because many people have inflated expectations of a leader, and when they fail personally they shift the responsibility onto the leader. Leaders, especially those who take on innovation and change, often meet accusations and criticism. It is important to learn to work with this feedback effectively, to understand that criticism can be constructive and to use it to improve. It is also important for a leader to learn to guard their heart against disappointment and offence.","Guarding your heart under criticism is an important part of any leader's life. Understanding yourself and your emotions helps you keep your inner balance even in difficult situations and under criticism, allowing you to feel emotions without letting them control your actions.","Remember why you do what you do. Focus on the goal and the vision that inspire you. This will help you overcome disappointment and stay positive. The ability to recognise other people's emotions, and empathy, can also help you understand why criticism arises. This can make you more tolerant of others' opinions. See criticism as a chance to improve, not as a personal attack. Ask yourself whether there is something useful in the criticism and how you can use it to grow. Do everything you can to have the support of people who understand and support you. They can help you approach criticism positively and keep your emotional balance.","Guarding your heart under criticism is key to remaining a confident leader and responding to situations with wisdom and calm.","An outstanding leader constantly works on their personal and professional growth. This may require learning new skills, adapting to change and sustaining their own motivation. They must keep learning, discovering new fields of knowledge and experience. There can be no pause in this process. It requires spending a certain amount of time and money. Such a leader always remains a student. I remember when I had already been a pastor and leader for some time and, as I thought, understood my work, after talking with Dr Bill Bassansky I felt that I knew and understood nothing at all. I shared this with Dr Bassansky, who by then was nearly eighty. He replied: «My dear, I feel as if I am only now being moved up from kindergarten to first grade.» Outstanding leaders are set on learning throughout their lives.","The price an outstanding leader pays may be high, but it can also lead to great success, influence and recognition. At first glance the difference between an experienced leader and an outstanding one is barely noticeable. But these things, barely noticeable to most people, make a huge difference between an experienced leader and an outstanding one.","A leader who exceeds expectations is one who is ready to surpass themselves. They conquer personal peaks of possibility and open new horizons of mastery. They strive to use and unlock their potential to the full in order to carry out their vision. Here leadership shifts from how we respond to various circumstances and challenges to who we ourselves become. The leader is no longer simply a leader in some position with certain duties; they themselves become a leader, and that changes things profoundly.","Embracing growth as the path to great success reflects the importance of constant self-improvement and openness to new opportunities. In today's world, where change happens fast, leadership requires a readiness to adapt and grow together with one's surroundings. Growth becomes a key part of success in many areas of life and career.","Improving yourself as a leader has a price and requires a constant search for opportunities for greater success. Our future is not free; it has its price. A simple principle applies here: we get as much as we invest. This applies to every area of life: relationships, business, study and leadership.","«With what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you: and unto you that hear shall more be given.» Mark 4:24.","Reaching the limits of your potential is an important goal for any leader or individual, because it means making the fullest use of your abilities and opportunities.","Getting the result you want often requires investment, whether of time, effort, knowledge or other resources. Whoever is ready to invest in a better future already recognises that paying the price today can bring more valuable results tomorrow. Your time and resources today belong not only to you today; they belong to your future. The question is how much we care about the future, enough to be willing to pay the price for it.","If you choose the cheapest third-class berth, you may save money now, but you miss the chance of a more comfortable, better travel experience. In the same way, investing in learning, development and personal growth can take you to a higher point in the future. Your knowledge and skills are the only capital that always stays with you, and the only capital that can pay huge dividends in your work.","In the end, what you get depends on what you invest. Investing in yourself can bring greater inner satisfaction, achievement and recognition.","If you choose a more expensive train ticket, you may travel in greater comfort and with a more pleasant experience. In the same way, investing in education and growth can create more opportunities and satisfaction in life.","It is important to understand that investing in yourself means investing in your own development and growth. Such preparation will let you shape your future more and achieve greater success.","So if we are ready to invest our resources in our own development and personal growth, we can expect more valuable results in the future, just as the ticket you choose decides your comfort and impressions on the journey.","Saving does not always lead to wealth. It can be the sign of a mindset limited by fear and doubt.","«There is that scattereth, and yet increaseth;","and there is that withholdeth more than is meet, but it tendeth to poverty.» Proverbs 11:24.","Successful leaders are not those who saved their resources but those who invested them wisely.","«Which do you think is stronger, knowledge or feeling?»","«Feeling!»","«Why?»","«Because although I know I owe Boris money, I have a feeling I won't pay him back.»","Our feeling that we don't want to invest today's resources for the sake of future success can slow down the growth of an outstanding leader in us. Desire, dream, achieve!"],["Creativity is often associated with creative professions or artistic people. But leadership can involve a great deal of creativity, even if the person is not a painter or an artist.","Creativity is the ability to think and act in unconventional ways, to find new and original ideas, solutions and approaches to tasks and problems. It shows itself in the ability to find unexpected ways of solving problems, to create new concepts, products or services, and to rethink and transform things that already exist.","Creativity can be applied in many areas of life, from art and science to business and everyday affairs. It helps find innovative solutions, expands possibilities and drives the growth of both the individual and society as a whole.","In today's world creativity is essential for success in any field. It helps people develop new ideas, create innovations and change the world around them for the better.","Nehemiah is an excellent example of a creative person. His story in the Old Testament shows how a creative approach can lead to great change and improvement.","Nehemiah learned that the walls of Jerusalem were broken down and the city lay in ruins. This stirred in him a desire to help rebuild the city, and he worked out a creative plan to restore the walls and protect the city.","Nehemiah showed his creativity in the following ways.","He carefully worked out a plan to rebuild the walls, dividing it into specific stages. This allowed effort to be focused and the goal reached faster.","Nehemiah involved the local people in rebuilding the walls. He used his leadership and creativity to unite people around a shared goal.","To protect the workers from enemies, Nehemiah devised a plan with armed guards: people held a weapon in one hand and built the wall with the other.","He worked skilfully with neighbouring peoples to secure the resources needed to rebuild the walls.","Nehemiah proved to be a creative and effective leader who was able to accomplish important tasks in difficult conditions. His story became a picture of how a creative approach can lead to great positive change and help achieve a goal.","Creative thinking lets you look at situations from a different angle, find unexpected connections and solve problems with original approaches. It is a kind of thinking that goes beyond standard patterns and pushes back the limits of what is possible.","Creative thinking can be extremely useful in a wide range of fields, from science and technology to art, business and serving God. It opens the door to new ideas, innovations and achievements. Such approaches can usually turn ordinary things into something amazing.","The ability to look at problems and tasks from unusual points of view widens the range of solutions and develops creative potential. It is important to learn to tolerate uncertainty and feel at ease in the zone of the unknown, so that creative ideas have a chance to flourish.","Creative thinking requires practice and development. Like any skill, it can be improved through training, experiment and openness to the new. It develops the person, helps avoid stagnation and unlocks potential in the most unexpected directions.","So creative thinking is a key factor for success in today's world, where innovation and originality are essential.","Generating ideas. The ability to come up with new ideas, which may be quite far removed from what is already known. Every project is first born as an idea and begins in the imagination. Everything we know in today's world once existed only in the imagination of its creators.","Generating ideas is an important process for a leader, helping to unlock potential and find innovative solutions in different areas of work. It can be especially important for leaders, since their role is to approach problems creatively and respond to challenges. A leader often faces challenges that cannot be solved by ordinary approaches and familiar methods. This calls for allowing yourself to consider different, even very original, ways forward. It is important to understand that even the most original ideas do not come from nowhere. The fuel for creativity is a wealth of information from different fields, constant learning and the experience of others. The more different scenarios our brain knows, the easier it is to come up with its own solution. Creative people learn from the creativity of others. Enrich your experience and imagination with the success stories of outstanding leaders, and you will be able to give birth to your own unique creative approach.","The ability to associate: the ability to find connections between different ideas, notions or concepts.","Yes, the ability to associate is an important part of creative thinking. It helps you find new and unexpected connections between different elements and generate original ideas. When a leader can see what different situations, problems or concepts have in common, they can develop new approaches and solutions that may be more effective and creative.","Adaptation: the ability to adapt ideas and solutions from other fields for use in a new context. At one point I noticed that many people saw the church as a place where believers gather who have deliberately withdrawn from the reality of modern life. Yet the Bible has many important teachings that concern not only spiritual growth but also success and growth in other areas of life. This question gave me no peace for a long time; I longed to tell everyone: God loves you, He has an answer to every problem, you are able to change your life. Then I had the idea of creating an educational course on the principles of success based on biblical teaching. This course gave many people the chance to get to know the Holy Scriptures and gain practical knowledge they could apply to succeed in different areas of life. It made it possible to open biblical principles to those who were not yet ready to come to church, and to give them a valuable tool for personal and professional growth. The course was different from church services; it was a kind of bridge between the church and people who had no interest in faith in God. It is an example of combining different directions and creating new content.","Risk and experiment: a readiness to take risks and try new ideas even when failure is possible. Looking for new methods and paths to success involves experimenting, so you need to be ready for the valuable experience of things that don't work. But the most important thing is that you stay open to the new and ready to keep going on your own path of fulfilling your potential. And even your mistakes become valuable capital of experience.","In one of his talks Dr Bassansky said: «What would you do in life if you were sure you could not fail?» These words still have a strong influence on me today, because most of the limits that stop us from creativity, decisiveness and carrying out our vision are not outside us but within. Only we can overcome our fears and doubts.","Creativity is built into the basic settings of every one of us. God created man in His own image and likeness, and He is the Creator. The first man, Adam, named all the animals and had the capacity for creativity.","«And out of the ground the LORD God formed every beast of the field, and every fowl of the air; and brought them unto Adam to see what he would call them: and whatsoever Adam called every living creature, that was the name thereof.» Genesis 2:19.","Every person can unlock their creativity and develop this divine gift in many areas of life. Creativity is the continuation of God's own trait within us. Don't limit yourself, and don't let the belief that you are incapable of outstanding, life-changing decisions rob you of your worth."],["Accepting yourself is an important, key part of the road to great success. We often tend to compare ourselves with others, feeling a lack or dissatisfaction with our achievements. But true success begins with inner harmony, faith in your abilities and accepting yourself as you are.","Every person has their own unique set of abilities, character and experience. By accepting ourselves and believing in our potential, we are able to bring out the best of what we have. Free of inner limits and doubts, we can direct our energy to reaching our goals and fulfilling our dreams. You need to believe that you are worthy of success, that as a leader you have a right to your own voice and opinion in carrying out the best purpose in this world. Your worth lies not only in achievements, success or material things. The worth of every person begins with the fact that they are, and with who they are. Simply the fact that we exist has incredible worth. Every person is unique, with their own story, experience, emotions and potential.","Sadly, in a world where importance is measured by achievements and material goods, it is easy to lose your bearings and forget the deep worth of every person simply for who they are. It is important to remember that every person makes their own unique contribution, that we are all connected and can bring positive change into the world simply by being who we are, and that we must recognise this worth in others and in ourselves.","Understanding your own worth can be made harder by various factors and obstacles.","A spiral of negative thoughts. An inner critic can stop you from seeing your worth realistically, deepening a sense of insecurity. A spiral of negative thoughts can be extremely harmful to our self-esteem and to our belief in our own worth. Sometimes the inner critic can be harsher and more negative than any outside critic. It hinders our growth and steals the courage to discover ourselves as people. Allow yourself not to be ideal or flawless; otherwise you have no chance of a fruitful life. No one in the world is perfect, and every one of us knows it. Yet sometimes we find it easier to be lenient with others than with ourselves. We often don't give ourselves the right to make mistakes and be imperfect. Change the spiral of your thoughts from negative ones to thoughts that bring life and strengthen you.","«For as he thinketh in his heart, so is he.» Proverbs 23:7.","Our thoughts are the source either of life, health, success and happiness, or of destruction and suffering. Sometimes, to change your life, it is enough to change your thoughts. Change the quality of your thoughts to ones that inspire you and build your confidence. Don't try to defeat negative thoughts by endlessly mulling them over in the hope of finding answers to every question and so gaining peace. Things are arranged so that as soon as you find answers to some thoughts, new ones arise. It is like trying to open a combination safe that changes its code the instant you enter the right numbers. It is a game of infinity, a circle with no way out. Only switching to other thoughts, a different setting, can resolve it.","«Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth.» 3 John 1:2.","Your thoughts are your area of responsibility. Start sowing seeds that will bear the fruit you want. Sow yourself with right convictions and let them take root. In the Bible you will find countless promises able to turn the negative into fruitful convictions that will set you free from limits.","«Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.","But his delight is in the law of the LORD; and in his law doth he meditate day and night.","And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.» Psalm 1:1–3.","Comparison with others. Comparing yourself with others can crush your self-esteem. Always remember that every person has their own unique path and development. You need to focus on your own goals, achievements and growth, not on other people. You have your own time to grow, discover your gifts and go through your own formation. Besides, your personal talents and leadership style may be fundamentally different from others', so the expectations of you will be different too. Focus on your personal growth and the achievements that fit your unique path to success.","It was a real trial for me to realise that I am different from most of the successful people I have, by God's grace, been fortunate to know. I very often heard: «If you don't keep a certain routine, or something like it, you will never succeed.» One respected teacher even told me: «If I visit someone and look into the wardrobe with their personal things and see that they are not folded in perfect order, that tells me this person is good for nothing.» If you've guessed what I'm getting at, that remark plunged me into despair. I even began to lose faith that I could really do anything good in this world. All because the things in my wardrobe can look like the universe at the dawn of creation. I have my own rhythm of life and my own approach to work, and if it differs from how even the most successful person in the world does things, that does not mean I cannot be a leader able to walk my own path and fulfil my unique potential.","The problem of comparison, I believe, may be why the children of outstanding parents can have huge problems in their lives: not only they themselves but the people around them may constantly compare them with their parents' successes. They may feel they live in the shadow of great ancestors. Simply because others think they are not like their famous relative, the truly unique and outstanding traits they do have can be written off. This creates confusion and a sense of having no talent. Discovering yourself is the main task for everyone.","Toxic relationships. Relationships in which you are constantly criticised or undervalued can undermine your belief in your own worth. A toxic relationship is an interaction between people that harms the mental, emotional and physical state of one or both partners. Such relationships can lead to stress, negative emotions, insecurity and even mental health problems. Here are signs that may point to a toxic relationship that needs to be dealt with at once.","Constant criticism. One or both sides constantly criticise the other, pushing them to feel unaccepted and dissatisfied. Criticism can be a form of psychological abuse. Besides, criticism creates a negative atmosphere that harms not only the one being criticised but also those who belittle others. It is no accident that the Bible so often shows us that criticism is behaviour God condemns. One of the best-known verses in the Bible is in the psalm we have already quoted:","«Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.» Psalm 1:1.","Criticism is a destructive force that can kill, so it is important to protect yourself from its negative influence. The best thing I have learned about this is to leave the toxic environment and let the critics enjoy whatever they spend their time on.","Intimidation and threats, control and manipulation, and anything else that creates a negative atmosphere and stress can also be toxic. I want to point out that however other people treat you or behave, responsibility for how you respond to their actions is yours. Only you have the right to decide whether anyone may cross the boundaries of your personal space. Likewise, your response should not be negative. I mean: don't answer criticism with criticism, or anger and insults with insults. Learn to stand up for yourself without losing peace in your heart. The Bible teaches us to love our enemies, even those who deliberately want to hurt us. A leader will always face this challenge, because leaders run into such things more than others. Learning to forgive, understanding your dignity and holding on to faith in your vision is the main challenge in fulfilling yourself as a leader. An experienced leader understands that a negative attitude to others, criticism and manipulation are the traits of ineffective people.","«Finally, be ye all of one mind, having compassion one of another, love as brethren, be pitiful, be courteous:","Not rendering evil for evil, or railing for railing: but contrariwise blessing; knowing that ye are thereunto called, that ye should inherit a blessing.","For he that will love life, and see good days, let him refrain his tongue from evil, and his lips that they speak no guile:","Let him eschew evil, and do good; let him seek peace, and ensue it.» 1 Peter 3:8–11.","According to Scripture, the quality of our life and our future depend not on how people treat us but on what thoughts fill our heart and on how we treat others. If you feel a relationship has become unbearable, consider distancing yourself from it. Your mental and emotional health matters.","Find people who support you, believe in you and help you feel good about yourself. Work on your growth and on strengthening your inner confidence. This will help you cope more easily with toxic situations.","Keeping a positive sense of yourself and your worth is an important part of preventing and overcoming toxic relationships.","Past hurts. Negative experiences from the past can leave a scar on your sense of your own worth. Negative memories, hurts or failures we have lived through can leave a deep mark on our sense of worth and self-esteem. These experiences can shape our inner beliefs about ourselves, how we see our competence and our ability to achieve.","Such past hurts can often become an obstacle on the road to success and personal growth. They can breed doubts about our abilities, block us from new opportunities and make us avoid risk.","It is important to work through and transform these hurts, to change how we see them into something positive and learn to find important lessons in them. This may take time and inner work, but it is an important step towards restoring your sense of worth and developing your ability to succeed.","Remember that negative experiences do not define your true worth and possibilities. You have the power to turn them into important lessons and resources for your own growth and for helping others. Your experience can become a valuable resource for supporting others. But don't let your past control your future. Although not every trial we face in life is an expression of God's will, they can be used for our improvement and growth.","Social norms and standards. By society's standards of success it may seem that you don't measure up, and this can change how you see your own worth.","Social norms and standards can greatly affect how we see our own worth and success. Society often sets certain expectations and standards that can create a sense of inadequacy or dissatisfaction if you don't meet them.","This can harm your self-esteem and confidence. For example, if you have not reached certain markers of success set by society, you may feel that your achievements are less important or insignificant.","It is important to understand that social standards should not define your worth. Your uniqueness and inner worth outweigh any outside demands. You have the right to set your own goals and paths to success, departing from accepted norms.","It is important to learn to set your own goals and define success by your personal values and needs, not only by social standards. Your worth and potential are unique, and you have the right to grow and succeed in your own way.","Perfectionism. Demanding that you always be flawless can stop you from seeing your achievements and worth.","Perfectionism can greatly affect how you see your own worth and success. Striving for flawlessness and constantly keeping up high standards can create extra stress and inner pressure and lead to dissatisfaction with your achievements.","Clearly, perfectionism can become an obstacle on the road to success, because it can keep you stuck in search of the perfect result instead of letting you focus on the process of growth and reaching your goals. What's more, constant dissatisfaction with yourself for not being perfect can lower your sense of worth and make you feel ineffective.","To overcome perfectionism, it is important to learn to accept yourself as you are, with all your strengths and weaknesses. It is important to understand that no one is perfect, and small flaws do not affect your overall worth. Develop your abilities and work on improving yourself, but allow yourself to make mistakes and learn from them.","It is also important to set realistic goals and understand that what matters more is the process of growth and striving for better, not reaching perfection. Make sure you see your achievements as the result of your work and effort, and that you deserve to feel proud of your successes.","Understanding your own worth is a process, and it is important to work on it, becoming convinced that you are a unique and valuable person whatever obstacles may arise. Allow yourself to be yourself, to seek your own path to success and to create an atmosphere in your life that fits your happiness. Life is not a rehearsal or a preparation for something that will come later. Life is now, and you will not have another one. So we have no right to spend it on what limits us and steals our confidence. What do you lose, and what do you risk, if you decide to allow yourself to be confident and not to stop despite every circumstance? I'll give you a simple answer: nothing but limits and a wasted life. Life is worth the risk of living, and I don't mean self-love or a helpless life chasing endless pleasures. I mean a purposeful life and your own values, a life full of meaning and true, pure feeling."],["We all have dreams and ideas about who we want to become, what we want to achieve and what success we want to have. But these dreams often stay at the level of ideas if we are unable to turn them into action. Now it is time to talk about how to move from ideas to action and create your own path to success.","Many people are content with being regarded as people of great potential, talented and smart. But these things only mean something when they are put into practice. What use is it that someone understands what is best, or has talents, if in real life it stays merely theoretical? When people say someone has potential, that is very good, but on the other hand it means they are not yet fulfilling it. It is better to be an actual leader than a potential one.","Setting goals. The first step to creating a successful path is to decide exactly what you want to achieve. It is important to set both short-term and long-term goals. If we don't know where we are going, it is hard to work out how to get there. Setting goals is the foundation of any successful path. Without a clear understanding of what you want to achieve, it is hard to direct your efforts the right way.","Defined goals help you understand what steps you need to take to reach the result you want. They give you a concrete action plan and reduce the chance of distraction.","Your goals must be achievable. Unattainable goals don't engage the creative process of imagination and faith in achieving them. The subconscious treats them as something purely theoretical. On the other hand, goals must be big enough. Simple goals, or ones without enough scale, don't provide the motivation needed to reach them. Let your goals be realistic but big enough to motivate you.","Planning action. Goals are already a step forward, but reaching them requires careful planning. Break your goals into smaller steps and define the specific actions you will take to reach each one. Goals without an action plan are only goals and differ little from daydreams.","«Ah, I feel like going to Paris again.»","«Have you been to Paris before?»","«No, but I've felt like going before.»","Planning will help you not depend on mood and inspiration, which are always fluctuating. Mood and inspiration should depend on our decisions, not the other way round. I'll say it again: don't ask yourself what you feel like doing; ask yourself what you want to get done. Inspiration will come along the way.","And the most interesting part is to act. Really act. It is important not only to plan but actually to take steps towards your goals. We often run into inner resistance, or put off acting, because we realise we will lose our comfort zone and may be taking a risk.","I won't say what year it was, but back when I had no idea how business works yet had a strong desire to change something in my life, especially financially, I took a few important steps. First of all, I understood that people with successful businesses knew something I didn't know at the time. So my plan was first to learn, and not only from theory but directly from people who own businesses. After a while I understood it was time to act. A good acquaintance of mine, a member of parliament, offered me a chance to make money selling land in an expensive, exclusive area outside Kyiv. He explained how things worked and suggested I take the first step. I had to take a risk and invest everything I had at the time. Before the first deal was due, I didn't sleep all night. At some point I began thinking of backing out so as not to risk losing what I had. In the morning I told him on the phone that I wasn't sure I should do it. Then he said something that changed my decision and helped me take a step that later gave me the experience of successful business. Having heard out all my doubts and reasoning, he replied: «Dima, I understand what you're talking about: it's the fear of the first steps. I remember when I started my business, I didn't sleep all night, nervous about taking the first step. But it's your business, and it's up to you whether to take the risk.» I realised this was the moment of truth: start acting or not. It opened doors for me to places where before I had only seen the façade.","But only action leads to results. Only real deeds bring results. «Faith without works is dead,» said the apostle James. Be a person who moves to practice, carrying out your goals step by step. This will make you a person of success.","I often hear people wonder why those they consider not especially clever achieve more success than the truly smart and talented. It is simply that some work hard to succeed while others only think about it.","Making choices. Your path to success may change, and it is important to be ready for that. Some decisions may turn out to be ineffective. Being able to choose change and adapt is a key part of creating your own successful path. Persistence is a very valuable quality, but it should not be used where time and effort are wasted on what doesn't work and doesn't bring you closer to the goal. Instead, redirect your energy and effort to what","is truly needed.","Once someone suggested the idea of creating our own radio programme. We gathered a team and began carrying out the project, expecting a certain result in spreading the preaching of the Gospel. After working on it for some time and spending considerable money and strength, I noticed that we could use this resource more effectively. The programme was interesting to us, but its impact was in question. So after careful analysis and study of the matter, I decided to drop the project. Some found it hard to let go of something into which so much time and effort had gone, and I met with misunderstanding from those who enjoyed going on air every Saturday. But for me it mattered more to stop investing in something that wasn't helping us reach our goals than to keep it just because we were used to doing it. Continuing would have meant even more expense and losing precious time. It helped us find more effective ways to make an impact.","Overcoming obstacles. Every path to success has its challenges and obstacles. It is important to understand that this is normal, and instead of giving up on our goals we need to look for ways to overcome them.","At the planning stage we don't always imagine what obstacles we may meet; many things come up unexpectedly. See obstacles as opportunities for growth and development. Your response to difficulties can decide the outcome. So set yourself on persistence and devotion to the work. Focus on opportunities and believe that solving the problem can lead to new opportunities or positive change. What's more, obstacles themselves often push us to look for new approaches and force us to act in ways we would not act in ordinary circumstances. To find a solution, we set out on a journey in search of different options, and this helps open new opportunities.","Not stopping. Reaching one goal is only the beginning. A successful path has no end, and it is important to keep growing and setting yourself new challenges.","Creating your own successful path is a practice that requires devotion, patience and faith in yourself. Even if the beginning is hard, the confidence that you are able to reach your goals can become the key to amazing opportunities and great success.","The success story of Kentucky Fried Chicken (KFC) is a true example of not stopping in the face of difficulty, and of how will and stubbornness can lead to impressive results.","At 65, Harland Sanders lost his work at his own restaurant. Left with limited money and a pension, he decided he was not ready to end his business career. Instead, he decided to use his recipe for fried chicken with secret herbs and spices, which he had been perfecting for many years.","Sanders hit the road, offering his recipe to restaurants across America. His idea was to take no upfront payment from restaurants but instead to receive a share of the sale of every piece of fried chicken.","That is how the story of the KFC franchise began. At first it was hard, and he was often turned down. His first steps were full of rejection and difficulty. But Sanders didn't stop. He overcame obstacles one after another.","In time his fried chicken recipe began to gain popularity. He opened new restaurants under the KFC brand, and in his lifetime the chain spread not only across the United States but beyond them.","Sanders kept working with KFC even after the chain became global. He took part in advertising campaigns and travelled to promote the brand. His image became known all over the world.","Today KFC is one of the best-known fast-food chains in the world. Sanders's success story shows that with will, devotion to your idea and an unbreakable spirit, even the hardest goals can be reached.","This story shows that even when difficulties seem insurmountable, it is important not to stop but to keep moving forward, crossing your own limits and turning negative circumstances into opportunities.","May your path be full of determination, faith and unbreakable will, and you will be able to create your own unique success story that inspires others to reach their own dreams."],["Full-scale leadership is the idea that a leader is not limited to the basic aspects of their role but goes beyond them to achieve maximum impact, effectiveness and growth.","It means that a leader is not limited to carrying out everyday duties but sets great goals and high standards. They are not content with the status quo and constantly strive for improvement, growth and innovation.","Striving for excellence. A leader always strives to reach a higher level in everything they do. They strive for excellence not only in their work but also in their own growth and relationships with others. Doing things just fine is what most people do. Let what sets you apart be the desire to do everything in the best way. I call it «high spirit»: a quality that begins inside you and shows in everything you do.","King Solomon was such a leader. His wisdom became famous not only through the deep sayings recorded in the Bible but also through his unique way of life.","«And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon concerning the name of the LORD, she came to prove him with hard questions.","And she came to Jerusalem with a very great train, with camels that bare spices, and very much gold, and precious stones: and when she was come to Solomon, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.","And Solomon told her all her questions: there was not any thing hid from the king, which he told her not.","And when the queen of Sheba had seen all Solomon's wisdom, and the house that he had built,","And the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel, and his cupbearers, and his ascent by which he went up unto the house of the LORD; there was no more spirit in her.","And she said to the king, It was a true report that I heard in mine own land of thy acts and of thy wisdom.","Howbeit I believed not the words, until I came, and mine eyes had seen it: and, behold, the half was not told me: thy wisdom and prosperity exceedeth the fame which I heard.» 1 Kings 10:1–7.","As the Bible story says, the queen was left breathless when she SAW the wisdom Solomon had. Everything Solomon did was excellent, done in the best way. In this sense, small differences make a big difference between good leaders and great ones, between the quality product we all want to have and the «almost the same» one that lacks quality.","A leader's «high spirit» begins inside them. You cannot achieve quality on the outside if you don't have it inside. I plan to say more about this in my next book, but for now I want to motivate you to start building and nurturing an excellent leader within yourself. Don't settle for a low level or poor quality for yourself. Compromise can harm how you feel and how you see yourself. Attention to detail completes the picture of your leadership and sets you apart from others. You are worth it.","Maximum impact. Full-scale leadership aims at the greatest possible positive impact on others. A leader seeks to bring positive change to the lives and work of others, spurring them on to better results.","A full-scale leader does not stop at themselves. They understand that their task is to spread their influence as far as possible for the sake of positive change in the lives of others. Being simply a good person is wonderful, but it is not enough for leadership. «Being a good person is not a profession»: become an influential leader. Don't wall yourself off from the world; go out to others and influence them. That is your domain, your place.","Besides that, expect excellence from others and motivate them towards it. Don't accept low quality or a poor attitude from others. Let them know that you will require their best. This will help them grow under your influence. They will be grateful to you if their lives change for the better. Your area of responsibility is your sphere of influence, so your rules and principles must apply there.","Finally, I'll note that a «high spirit» in leadership includes outward appearance, manner of speaking and the quality of relationships within the team.","Developing the team. A leader invests time and effort in developing their team. They help every team member grow and develop, providing support, training and opportunities for self-improvement. The fruit of a true leader is new leaders who grow up under their influence. They inspire others to achieve.","A team is an essential condition for reaching and fulfilling a great vision. A leader's influence will be significant if they build a team of like-minded people. It is the team that reaches the highest level of authority and widens the bounds of influence. The work can continue after the leader, because they have left disciples behind. In the Gospels we see that the disciples of Jesus Christ became the world's foremost preachers and reformers, who in turn prepared new leaders for a new generation. This principle is reflected in the words of the apostle Paul:","«And the things that thou hast heard of me among many witnesses, the same commit thou to faithful men, who shall be able to teach others also.» 2 Timothy 2:2.","Building a team and training new leaders play an important role in spreading vision and influence and in reaching more people.","This helps scale your influence. By forming a strong, motivated team and training new leaders, you can multiply your influence. Each new leader or team member can become a channel for passing on vision, values and ideals to different groups and places.","Variety of influence: different leaders and teams can reach different audiences and groups of people. This allows your vision and ideas to reach different social strata, cultures and communities. By creating local groups, building a team and training new leaders in different places, you create local «hubs» of influence. These groups can work on shared goals aimed at fulfilling your vision. In our church, City of Light Kyiv, this purpose is served by small groups that meet regularly for fellowship and to support one another.","The team and leaders can spread your ideas and message in different formats adapted to the needs and realities of different audiences. This helps draw in more people and make a greater impact. Training new leaders and building a team reflect your ability to teach and to learn together with others. This builds a strong, mutually supportive environment that helps achieve shared goals.","The team and leaders can create a system that lets you automate and optimise actions to fulfil the vision. This makes it possible to influence more people without increasing resources.","By building a strong team and training new leaders, you create your own «centre of movement» that moves together towards great goals. This shared work ensures that the vision spreads and has a positive impact on the greatest number of people.","Unity is an extremely important factor in a team's success. When team members work together in unity, they achieve great results.","Unity helps team members direct their efforts towards a common goal. Everyone steps in the same direction, which boosts productivity and effectiveness. People in the team then work together, combining their skills and knowledge to solve problems and overcome challenges. Cooperation leads to creative solutions and new possibilities, where everyone can show their unique qualities and talents.","Unity in a team creates an atmosphere of support and mutual help. People support one another, helping every member of the group.","Unity in a team creates a favourable atmosphere for developing and fulfilling individual and shared ambitions, which raises each member's motivation. They work together to find solutions and approaches quickly.","Unity affects the team's overall productivity. When everyone works in the same direction, the work gets done faster and more effectively.","Unity in a team is a process that requires mutual understanding, openness to other points of view and a readiness to work together towards goals.","It is impossible to imagine a football team playing successfully when each player plays only for himself, tries to draw attention to himself while neglecting the shared victory, and generally plays only by his own rules. Even if the team were made up of the world's best football stars, it would not succeed, because football is a team game, and victory or defeat will always be shared.","Strategic thinking. Full-scale leadership involves the ability to see the big picture, understand long-term consequences and develop strategies that will help reach future goals.","A leader's main task is the ability to consider not only current tasks but also how they affect the overall goal and development of the organisation or project. They must always be looking to the future. When they don't give enough attention to the long view, the quality of their work can suffer. You need to plan your time skilfully and wisely and delegate duties, so as not to lose the main focus on strategic questions. This is described very clearly in the story of Moses, when he became so absorbed in solving the tasks and issues of the people of Israel in the wilderness that he began to lose the main thing: teaching the Law and leading the way to the promised land. His father-in-law came to his aid and gave him very wise advice:","«13 And it came to pass on the morrow, that Moses sat to judge the people: and the people stood by Moses from the morning unto the evening. 14 And when Moses' father in law saw all that he did to the people, he said, What is this thing that thou doest to the people? why sittest thou thyself alone, and all the people stand by thee from morning unto even? 15 And Moses said unto his father in law, Because the people come unto me to enquire of God: 16 When they have a matter, they come unto me; and I judge between one and another, and I do make them know the statutes of God, and his laws. 17 And Moses' father in law said unto him, The thing that thou doest is not good. 18 Thou wilt surely wear away, both thou, and this people that is with thee: for this thing is too heavy for thee; thou art not able to perform it thyself alone. 19 Hearken now unto my voice, I will give thee counsel, and God shall be with thee: Be thou for the people to God-ward, that thou mayest bring the causes unto God: 20 And thou shalt teach them ordinances and laws, and shalt shew them the way wherein they must walk, and the work that they must do. 21 Moreover thou shalt provide out of all the people able men, such as fear God, men of truth, hating covetousness; and place such over them, to be rulers of thousands, and rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens: 22 And let them judge the people at all seasons: and it shall be, that every great matter they shall bring unto thee, but every small matter they shall judge: so shall it be easier for thyself, and they shall bear the burden with thee. 23 If thou shalt do this thing, and God command thee so, then thou shalt be able to endure, and all this people shall also go to their place in peace.","24 So Moses hearkened to the voice of his father in law, and did all that he had said. 25 And Moses chose able men out of all Israel, and made them heads over the people, rulers of thousands, rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens. 26 And they judged the people at all seasons: the hard causes they brought unto Moses, but every small matter they judged themselves.» Exodus 18:13–26.","I want to underline these words: «thou shalt teach them ordinances and laws, and shalt shew them the way wherein they must walk, and the work that they must do». In other words, every organisation or group can exist only for the sake of some future goal; otherwise its growth loses its meaning. It must create, let's call it, a product: something it makes through shared effort. It must also give its members the chance to fulfil themselves, grow and develop, and become attractive to new people. Under these conditions everyone understands why they are part of the community. Something is created that unites everyone for a common goal and future. If the great vision disappears, along with the prospect of shared growth and personal interest, the uniting factor disappears too. This is exactly what the strategic leader must ensure, together with the other members of the team.","A true strategic leader takes many factors into account and helps steer the whole team towards shared goals, making the right big decisions that have a long-term impact."],["At last I have come to the point where I can shine a light on the most powerful passage in Nehemiah's story. In my view it is the quintessence of everything Nehemiah did, the essence of his work as a leader:","«Ye see the distress that we are in, how Jerusalem lieth waste, and the gates thereof are burned with fire: come, and let us build up the wall of Jerusalem, that we be no more a reproach.» Nehemiah 2:17.","This is a quotation from the book of Nehemiah, which tells how Nehemiah, after returning to Jerusalem, sees the ruin and decay of the city. He calls his team to join in rebuilding the city and its broken walls. The quotation reflects not only an understanding of the situation and the reality of the problems but also a confidence that through shared effort they will be able to restore the city and be rid of the disgrace.","A leader who inspires achievement helps raise the bar of expectations, unlocks the potential of others and contributes to the team's overall success. Vision is one of the most important parts of successful leadership. A clear, carefully thought-out vision can set the direction for a team's growth, create motivation to reach goals and inspire others to great achievements. A vision must be tangible, inspiring and positive. It must give people the sense that by putting effort into these goals they will achieve something meaningful. A vision must be specific, pointing directly to what is to be achieved. It must be easy to understand and convey the main message at once.","Today, when our country is in the middle of the cruellest trial known in human history, war, leadership takes on special significance. Hard times need true leaders more than ever. When a country or society faces severe challenges, it is important that leaders rise to the task and ensure the right response and recovery. God calls ordinary people like Nehemiah. Hearing about the state of Jerusalem and its ruins, he did not stand aside. Nehemiah felt God's call and decided to take responsibility for rebuilding the city. He gathered a team, worked out a plan, overcame difficulties and enemies, and in the end rebuilt the city of Jerusalem.","Today too there are many challenges and problems facing modern society. God may call each of us to help solve them and to become a leader who brings positive change. Our actions, even small ones, can matter a great deal to the people around us.","If you feel a desire and an ability in yourself to help improve the situation, let Nehemiah's story inspire you to act. Change begins with our desire and our decision to take responsibility. You can be the leader who brings positive change and helps make the world around you better.","God has always needed a person to carry out His plan of salvation in hard and important times. Every person has the opportunity to serve and do God's will through their actions, deeds and dealings with others. Your readiness to help and to be a channel for God's plans can matter greatly, not only to you but to others around you. God truly works through us when we give Him our hearts and lives. Today He calls us to become the Nehemiahs of our time, to rebuild our country and make it flourishing and happy.","An inspiring leader has a clear vision and a passion to fulfil it. They believe in the importance of change and strive for improvement. By changing people's emotional mood and motivation, as Nehemiah did, great success is possible.","A true leader understands that the main motive of their vision is compassion and empathy for those who need their support. The story of David and his time in the cave with rejected and unfortunate people is a striking example of how a leader can turn failure into opportunity and even raise true leaders from such people.","This story is found in the First Book of Samuel, chapter 22. David was being pursued by King Saul and his army, and he fled to the cave of Adullam. There he was joined by people who were neglected and rejected by society: debtors and the discontented. These people were in a wretched state and felt like outcasts.","David took them in and set out for the Judean wilderness, where together they began to form their team. David trusted them, helped them and taught them. As a result, these rejected and cast-off people became true heroes and leaders. They became David's devoted followers and eventually helped him take the throne.","«David therefore departed thence, and escaped to the cave Adullam: and when his brethren and all his father's house heard it, they went down thither to him.","And every one that was in distress, and every one that was in debt, and every one that was discontented, gathered themselves unto him; and he became a captain over them: and there were with him about four hundred men.» 1 Samuel 22:1–2.","This story underlines how important the leader's role is in recognising and developing the potential of every person, even those who seemed to have no chance. David saw possibilities in these people, trusted them and taught them, and this allowed them to flourish and become influential leaders. The story reminds us that sometimes those who may look like failures or rejects have the potential to become true heroes and achieve great things under the influence of the right leadership and inspiration. David saw potential in these people even when others did not believe in them. His ability to see the worth in each person and inspire them to great deeds made them the true heroes of his story.","True leaders are not limited by their position or role. They believe in every person's potential and know how to discover and develop it. An inspiring leader helps others see in themselves possibilities they can make real.","By inspiring others, you help them understand that their possibilities are limitless, that they can grow, develop and reach great heights. Your ability to see in people not only what is there now but also the potential they can unlock makes you a true leader of positive change.","Remember that your ability to inspire and support others can turn ordinary situations into unforgettable experiences of growth and achievement. May your mission as a leader always be accompanied by a desire to develop others, faith in their potential and confidence that together you can do amazing things."],["Leadership is a journey with no end. It is a tireless movement towards new heights, achievements and opportunities. This book has helped us look at the key aspects of leadership, from inner motivation to influencing others. But this is only the beginning of your own journey as a leader.","Let the end of this book be the beginning of your next stage of growth and development. Remember that leadership is not only about influencing others but also about constant self-improvement. Keep exploring new ideas, developing your skills, learning from your mistakes and inspiring others by your example.","Your road of leadership can lead to amazing achievements that will affect not only you personally but the whole world around you. May your will to learn, your devotion and your unbreakable faith in yourself always go with you on this unending journey. The leader's road never ends; it always leads forward to new opportunities and achievements.","Thank you for joining me on this journey. I wish you unforgettable leadership, great achievements and inexhaustible motivation!"]];